Z||000000||HummelHund||04-22-2001||03:48 PM||||Looking at my engine (2.5L) this afternoon, I noticed that I do not have the tube that runs from the bottom of the intake snorkel to the exhaust manifold(the Haynes manual calls it a heat stove tube). Is this a bad thing? Should I just cover the hole up or go junkyard shopping for a tube? Could this be causing stumbling or idle problems? <BR>Thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||5
Z||000001||c m west||04-22-2001||05:02 PM||||it means it will not activate your thermac valve, therby creating problems for cold start up - you WILL NOT pass smog without this tube<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnt671||04-22-2001||07:27 PM||||Most auto parts stores sell these cheap, and it only takes a few minutes to put the tube on.  My 84 takes a 2 in. dia. tube.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
